I've read many boasts here lately about high-score ascensions (incl.
a claim of 18M pts) but what about a low score ascension? Seems to me
that's equally, if not more challenging.

The easy part is: don't collect gems (except a few to ward off u's),
keep your pets and everyone else away from you when standing on the
endgame altar, drop all your stuff besides the AY when you #offer it.

The other stuff that gets factored in is your *real* experience (i.e Xp
gained by whacking monsters, rather than by other means) and the number
of levels visited. You can keep down the levels visited by not going to
the mines, not going on the quest (so you have to wish for the bell, and
maybe the candles as well.) To boost your HP while keeping your real Xp
down, you have to run away from all monsters except wraiths and succubi,
and quaff lots of PoGL.

So: how about some low-score boasts here? (I don't plan to participate
in this challenge myself: I only ascended once, and that was after much
huffing and puffing. 5M pts, incidentally.) What do you suppose is the
theoretical lowest possible score?
